This folder bundles a Piper text-to-speech voice, run via the sherpa-onnx
runtime, for SignVox's offline neural voice (PLAN.md §6.4).

## Voice: en_US-ljspeech-medium (vits-piper-en_US-ljspeech-medium)

Trained on the LJ Speech Dataset (Keith Ito, https://keithito.com/LJ-Speech-Dataset/),
which is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN. See vits-piper-en_US-ljspeech-medium/MODEL_CARD.

This voice was deliberately chosen over other available Piper voices (e.g.
en_US-lessac-medium) specifically because its training data has no usage
restrictions — some other Piper voices are trained on datasets (e.g. the
Lessac Blizzard 2013 corpus) whose license explicitly forbids commercial
use or redistribution in a shipped product. Do not substitute a different
bundled voice without checking its MODEL_CARD's dataset license first.

## Piper (voice architecture / training toolkit)

https://github.com/rhasspy/piper — MIT License.

## sherpa-onnx (on-device inference runtime used to run this voice)

https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx — Apache License 2.0.
